{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cee1NzqUwB8tzKEBc1hvv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014y2GswmFzTr1GZSSEzx52B","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/diytechy/.claude/projects/-Users-diytechy-Documents-ai-template/memory/worker-lane-close-ritual-traps.md","content":"---\nname: worker-lane-close-ritual-traps\ndescription: Three traps a worker lane hits at C6 close — Deliverable must stay empty until the close commit, and two test reds that are trunk's or pre-existing, not yours\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nMeasured on the WI-572 lane, 2026-09-01. All three recur for any worker lane.\n\n**1. Fill `## Deliverable` ONLY in the close commit.** `check_trajectory` errors\n`R-A <WI>: status=active (open) but the Deliverable is non-empty (an open WI's\nDeliverable is filled only at close)`, and the pre-commit hook REJECTS the\ncommit. This collides with the standing-state rule (\"land the spec's\nContext/Deliverable edits early\"): the Context half is safe, the Deliverable\nhalf is not. It reads the file ON DISK, so staging around it does not help —\npark the filled spec outside the repo and restore it at close.\n**Why:** a filled Deliverable is the close signal; an open row carrying one is\na lie about its own state.\n**How to apply:** land Context early; keep the Deliverable in the scratchpad\nuntil the one commit that also clears `specref` and runs `spec_move.py`.\n\n**2. Amending a settled spine row reds `test_derive_stage.py::\ntest_this_repo_s_committed_stage_is_current`.** `docs/stage` is derived over\nSETTLED rows, so amending an `Approved` row moves its fingerprint. Do NOT\nregenerate: `docs/stage` is a declared generated artifact, every commit that\never wrote it is trunk-side bookkeeping, and the commit bar's own\n`derived-stage --check` SKIPS on a work branch. Verify it is benign by\nregenerating in a scratch worktree — only `fingerprint` and the as-of stamp\nshould move, every rung byte-identical.\n\n**3. Closing the LAST active claim reds `test_wi_convert.py::\ntest_the_live_registry_round_trips_in_whichever_home_is_authoritative`** on\n`docs/work/cancelled/README.md: does not start with a +++ frontmatter fence`.\nWith a claim in flight the converter refuses by name (`drained-stop`) and the\ntest passes on that branch; drained, it runs the real folder round-trip and\nmeets a README the walker does not skip. Pre-existing — reproduces at trunk\ncommits with no `docs/work/active/` at all.\n\n**How to apply (2 and 3):** report both reds with their provenance rather than\nchasing them or claiming green. Bisect the single test in a `git worktree` at\nthe prior commit — that is what separates \"inherited\" from \"caused\", and it is\ncheap. Related: [[supervised-loop-macos-operating-lessons]],\n[[repointing-approved-spine-during-rework]].\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9636,"cache_read_input_tokens":161164,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9636},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8876d3e3-9ead-4365-844a-04fd0bdeb9de","uuid":"f5632a7a-64e9-4898-9870-00560941f62b","request_id":"req_011Cee1NyrSyDx5aGTj919EP"}
