{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cee1RzDrke5MGiiB66tj8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"WI-572 is closed on its branch. Summary:\n\n## What I found and did\n\nThe mechanism (the merge-slot refusal, the first-approval adjudication arm, the derived `{aftermath}` slot, the doctrine) had already landed in four commits. I completed the row with four more:\n\n- **`7021e4e1`** — the two reference surfaces (`enforcement-audit.md`, `registry-machinery-reference.md`) and the IF-090/IF-091 module contracts.\n- **`a68cc52a`** — re-pointed two registry rows *my own branch's code* made stale: `LLR-158`'s `code_symbol`/`Detail` and `IF-091`'s requestors. Both warns were introduced by this branch; both are gone.\n- **`21902ac2`** — the C6 close: Deliverable, `specref` cleared, brief regenerated, `spec_move.py`.\n- **`b25660e3`** — the provenance of the second red.\n\n## Two judgement calls worth flagging\n\n**I amended an `Approved` spine row.** The standing constraint forbids *flipping* a Status, not amending — and the WI-553 precedent says a lane re-points its own staleness in-lane rather than deferring. I verified this with the row's own new mechanism rather than assuming: `staged_approval_acts → []`, `lane_approval_refusal → None`, while `staged_spine_amendments` reports `LLR-158`. So the amendment adjudication gets raised for it at merge — this lane's edit is the first customer of the arm the lane shipped.\n\n**The suite is not green, and I did not make it green.** Full run: **3257 passed, 1 failed, 24 skipped in 557 s**; the smoke tier surfaces a second. Both are recorded with evidence, not absorbed:\n\n1. `test_derive_stage.py::test_this_repo_s_committed_stage_is_current` — my amendment moved `docs/stage`'s input digest. Regenerating in a scratch worktree moves **only** the fingerprint and as-of stamp; every rung is byte-identical. Regenerating is the trunk lane's act (the commit bar's own `derived-stage --check` skips on work branches), so I left it.\n2. `test_wi_convert.py::...round_trips...` — my close drained the last active claim, moving the test off its \"claim in flight\" branch onto a folder walk that chokes on `docs/work/cancelled/README.md`. **Reproduces at `9eaeac93`, before WI-572 was claimed** — inherited, not caused.\n\nI bisected each in a `git worktree` rather than reasoning about it, because that's what separates \"inherited\" from \"caused.\"\n\nThree follow-ons are named in the log fragment rather than smuggled in: narrowing the owner's brief to held rungs, giving the `docs/stage` test the work-branch exemption its `--check` twin has, and the `wi_convert` README skip.\n\nTwo untracked items are deliberately left: `.venv` (a symlink to another repo's venv — the `.venv/` ignore pattern doesn't match symlinks) and the iteration log, which the loop commits itself as `telemetry:`. Nothing on this branch is pushed — `push = \"human\"`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":402,"cache_read_input_tokens":174125,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":402},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8876d3e3-9ead-4365-844a-04fd0bdeb9de","uuid":"b1fd19e6-eb32-4c76-bfd3-f640be06ea67","request_id":"req_011Cee1Ry5u4zQXMib3JUsjp"}
